  "body": "Sibling of #4151, left out of the fix for it.\n\n`extensionHere` in internal/agent/gone.go decides whether Claude Code's or Codex's CLI folder is still read by an editor extension (`anthropic.claude-code`, `openai.chatgpt`, `saoudrizwan.claude-dev`). It looks only under `~/.<editor>/extensions`. A portable VS Code (`code-portable-data/extensions` beside the `.app` on a Mac, `<install>/data/extensions` on Windows and Linux, Scoop included) keeps its extensions in its data folder. So a user whose only reader of `~/.claude` or `~/.codex` is the extension in a portable VS Code can see that CLI listed as gone (\"CLI not found\") on a Mac or Linux. Windows is never gone for shared folders, so it isn't affected there.\n\nThe fix for #4151 adds `vscodePortableData(kind)`, which finds the portable data folder through the launcher on PATH or, on a Mac, through the app folders. `extensionHere` (or `cliHeld`) could also look in `<data>/extensions` for each VS Code kind (stable, Insiders, VSCodium).\n\nA test needs a portable layout (fixtures as in internal/agent/vscode_portable_test.go) with the extension installed only there, and must expect the CLI not to be gone.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
