   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T21:49:44Z",
   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/4672-portable-vscode-extension-detection), commit [d5e7c3ab5](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/d5e7c3ab59dbdbed7b5ffd291fc69117acb4bbe7), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe extension check now reuses the existing portable data-directory finder for VS Code Stable, Insiders and VSCodium, in addition to standard extension directories. This keeps Claude, Codex and Cline from being marked CLI-missing while their installed portable extension still reads the shared folder. The Windows shared-folder rule is unchanged; the shared extension check also informs Codex async-compaction detection.\n\nTemporary portable launchers and extension folders reproduce the three false missing states on the base. Parent race tests pass the three agents, all three editor channels, missing/unrelated-extension controls and existing shared-folder/async-compaction checks. Agent vet and the full `nogui` build pass. Native macOS and Windows and the full suite were not run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
